---
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

/** Date of the last review recorded on this page. Update it whenever the checks are redone. */
const lastReviewed = '2026-09-17';
const contact = [site.socials.linkedin, site.socials.github];
---

<Layout title="Accessibility" description={`Accessibility statement for ${site.url.replace('https://', '')}: target level, what was tested, and how to report a problem.`}>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose a11y">
      <p class="eyebrow">Accessibility</p>
      <h1>Accessibility statement</h1>
      <p>
        I want everyone to be able to read this site, whatever their device, browser or assistive
        technology. This page says what it aims for, what has been checked, and how to tell me
        when something gets in the way.
      </p>

      <h2>Target</h2>
      <p>
        The site aims to meet the <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/">Web Content Accessibility
        Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2</a> at level <strong>AA</strong>. It is a small static site: two pages,
        no forms, no video, no third-party widgets.
      </p>

      <h2>What has been checked</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Keyboard only.</strong> Every page can be used without a mouse: a "Skip to content"
          link appears on the first Tab, focus is always visible, the theme button and the expandable
          work history work with Enter and Space, and nothing traps focus.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Screen reader.</strong> Landmarks (header, navigation, main, footer), heading order,
          link and button names, and the accessibility tree were reviewed with VoiceOver on macOS.
          The animated line under my name is hidden from assistive technology and replaced by a static
          list of the same words.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Colour contrast, light and dark theme.</strong> Every text colour was measured against
          every background it sits on. All pairs are above 4.5:1; body text is above 12:1 in both themes.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Motion.</strong> When the operating system asks for reduced motion, animations and
          hover movements are switched off and the typing effect stays still. Without JavaScript the
          content is fully visible: the typing line shows its first word and the work history opens as
          plain disclosure widgets.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Structure.</strong> One <code>h1</code> per page, sequential headings, semantic lists
          and landmarks, a declared page language, and no information conveyed by colour alone (the current page in the navigation is underlined as well as coloured).
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Known limitations</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The short line under my name contains emoji; screen readers announce their names.</li>
        <li>External links open in a new tab, which is stated by the browser rather than in the link text.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Tell me about a problem</h2>
      <p>
        If something on this site is hard to use, I would like to know. Reach me on{' '}
        {contact.map((c, i) => (
          <>
            {i > 0 && ' or '}
            <a href={c.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{c.label}</a>
          </>
        ))}
        , and say which page and what you were trying to do. I will answer and fix what I can.
      </p>

      <p class="muted">Last reviewed on {lastReviewed}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .a11y { max-width: 68ch; }
  .a11y h2 { margin-top: 2rem; }
</style>
